NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The basic Svelte app example to get started with the TanStack svelte-store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"store.ts"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createStore } from '@tanstack/svelte-store';\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Svelte files too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\nexport function updateState(animal: 'cats' | 'dogs') {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App.svelte"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n\timport Increment from \"./Increment.svelte\";\n\timport Display from \"./Display.svelte\";\n</script>\n\n\n<h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n<p>Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends like cats or dogs</p>\n<Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n<Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n<Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n<Display animal=\"cats\" />","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Display.svelte"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n    import { useSelector } from '@tanstack/svelte-store';\n    import { store } from './store';\n    \n    const {animal}: { animal: 'cats' | 'dogs' } = $props()\n    const count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[animal]);\n</script>\n    \n<!-- This will only re-render when `state[animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render -->\n<div>{ animal }: { count.current }</div>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStore"},{"type":"text","value":" remains available as a deprecated alias to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Increment.svelte"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n    import { updateState } from './store';\n    \n    const { animal }: { animal: 'cats' | 'dogs' } = $props()\n</script>\n    \n<button onclick={() => updateState(animal)}>My Friend Likes { animal }</button>","lang":"html"}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe basic Svelte app example to get started with the TanStack svelte-store.\n\n**store.ts**\n```ts\nimport { createStore } from '@tanstack/svelte-store';\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Svelte files too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\nexport function updateState(animal: 'cats' | 'dogs') {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**App.svelte**\n```html\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n\timport Increment from \"./Increment.svelte\";\n\timport Display from \"./Display.svelte\";\n</script>\n\n\n<h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n<p>Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends like cats or dogs</p>\n<Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n<Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n<Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n<Display animal=\"cats\" />\n```\n\n\n**Display.svelte**\n```html\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n    import { useSelector } from '@tanstack/svelte-store';\n    import { store } from './store';\n    \n    const {animal}: { animal: 'cats' | 'dogs' } = $props()\n    const count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[animal]);\n</script>\n    \n<!-- This will only re-render when `state[animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render -->\n<div>{ animal }: { count.current }</div>\n```\n\n`useStore` remains available as a deprecated alias to `useSelector`.\n\n**Increment.svelte**\n```html\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n    import { updateState } from './store';\n    \n    const { animal }: { animal: 'cats' | 'dogs' } = $props()\n</script>\n    \n<button onclick={() => updateState(animal)}>My Friend Likes { animal }</button>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\nid: quick-start\n---\n\nThe basic Svelte app example to get started with the TanStack svelte-store.\n\n**store.ts**\n```ts\nimport { createStore } from '@tanstack/svelte-store';\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Svelte files too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\nexport function updateState(animal: 'cats' | 'dogs') {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**App.svelte**\n```html\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n\timport Increment from \"./Increment.svelte\";\n\timport Display from \"./Display.svelte\";\n</script>\n\n\n<h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n<p>Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends like cats or dogs</p>\n<Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n<Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n<Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n<Display animal=\"cats\" />\n```\n\n\n**Display.svelte**\n```html\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n    import { useSelector } from '@tanstack/svelte-store';\n    import { store } from './store';\n    \n    const {animal}: { animal: 'cats' | 'dogs' } = $props()\n    const count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[animal]);\n</script>\n    \n<!-- This will only re-render when `state[animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render -->\n<div>{ animal }: { count.current }</div>\n```\n\n`useStore` remains available as a deprecated alias to `useSelector`.\n\n**Increment.svelte**\n```html\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n    import { updateState } from './store';\n    \n    const { animal }: { animal: 'cats' | 'dogs' } = $props()\n</script>\n    \n<button onclick={() => updateState(animal)}>My Friend Likes { animal }</button>\n```\n"}
